From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:08:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Gate check: a seat with no referral code yet gets one, so the
 code branch can be asked
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's 58157: the third gate case (a subscribed inviter's code
admits) could not be run, because the newest fictional seats are
subscribed but had never had their code read, and so had none. The
route refused („has no referral code yet … pick another seat"), and the
seat ids that do have a code could not be relayed to the tester.

A member's code is minted on first read (getOrCreateReferralCode); a
seat's is now minted the same way when the gate check asks for it. It
still never leaves the server, and anybody who is not a test seat is
still refused before anything is minted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
